# Language-agnostic baseline. Stack-specific ignores get added once
# the stack is chosen in design.

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
\#*\#

# Secrets / local env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Claude Code (local settings, history, allowlist — mostly personal).
# Drop the trailing slash so the negation below can re-include a
# specific file; with `.claude/` git short-circuits at the
# directory and ignores the !.claude/foo line.
.claude/*
# Team-shared Claude Code config that SHOULD be in version control:
!.claude/settings.json
# Project files the global skills keep here. Without these lines each is
# silently never committed (CFG-0734).
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/bump.json
!.claude/code-pairs.json
!.claude/pr-workflow
!.claude/debt-sweep.json
# No `!.claude/workflow.md` here, deliberately. `workflow.md` § 1 forbids a
# per-project workflow, and reserving the path reads as a prescription to
# create one. That file was also the trigger of `/app-workflow`, the
# predecessor `workflow.md` replaced, retired 2026-09-28.

# Logs / runtime
*.log
*.pid
*.sock

# Coverage / sanitizers
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov
coverage.*
.coverage
lcov.info

# Core dumps
core
core.*
*.core
vgcore.*

# Scratch
scratch/
tmp/
Screenshot_*.png
screenshot*.png

# Roadmap ID counter — derived per-machine cache, not source.
# True high-water mark is the highest ID across ROADMAP.md +
# CHANGELOG.md + docs/roadmap/*.md (roadmap-format.md § 3.5.1).
.roadmap-counter
